 ALPHA TESTING STAGE
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
0.1    First alpha release.
       Released: 04-Jul-93

0.2    Added more stuff.
       Released: 08-Jul-93

0.3    BUG -- Timer code was causing gurus - fixed.
       Released: 11-Jul-93

0.4    More control codes, better line shutdown.
       ExpandCC -- Totally changed params.  Now uses struct CCArgs.
       				 Added better argument handling.
       				 Added C formatting support.
       Released: 12-Jul-93

0.5    Serial seems to be working now.
       Lines using serial are able to exit :)
       More ARexx commands.
       Fixed problems with Fifo/Serial input - Nasty stuff...
       Released: 22-Jul-93

0.6    Get Yes/No stuff done - I'm off on holiday :)
       Various bug fixes
       Released: 01-Aug-93

0.7    Fixed SaveUser a bit
       Added NiceName to Arexx list!
       Released: 03-Oct-93

0.8    Lots of new stuff!
       ENV variables done.
       Each line now has it's own timer.device.
       GetChar checks carrier every second (will also handle timeouts..)
       New window when initializing and shutting down.
       Main PIPELINE screen vapourised!
       Startup also runs programmes when PL is ready.
       Added WRITELOG to ARexx and library.
       Opens pipeutil.library on startup.
       Released: 10-Nov-93

0.9    Added more control to ENV vars
       Timer fixed in main loop.  Now calls every 60 secs.
       Timer wasn't obtaining the semaphores - naughty routine fixed...
       General cleanup of timer stuff.
       Added QUITPL to Rexx.
       Added REGINFO and COPYRIGHT to Rexx.
       Added/Moved DisplayFile to library which now tries several
          combinations of filename before giving up.
       Added carrier checking to the CLI interface (Whoops..)
       Added high 8-bit lookup conversion!!
       Passed some extra stuff to the library for future IO fun - no more
          nasty patching!
       Fixed StartPL to fill in the realbaud rate
       Fixed bug in SET/GET UserData
       PAW can now be run via workbench with project icons
       Released: 13-Nov-93

0.10   Finally added some chat stuff.
       Added StartChat and ChatWrite to library.
       Added StopChat to library.
       Added function key support to PAW.
       Wrote SimpleChat - very simple 2 colour chat program.
       Released: 14-Nov-93

0.11   Fixed several bugs.
       Added OpenTextFile into the library.
       Started the user editor.  Not finished yet but mostly there...
       Finished the program editor.
       Released: 19-Nov-93

0.12   Removed LOCAL option from the environmental variable commands.  It
          was causing crashes if it wasn't supplied!
       Added stuff to PUTONLINE, HANGUP and INITLINE that now modify the
          users structure before saveing and removing.
       Users cannot send ^C to doors now.
       Wrote code to give users the right amount of minutes when they call.
       Forgot to add checking to GetChar to see whether PL was quitting or
          not!  Fixed now...
       Changed DoorControl to write the door's return code to the log file.
       Added the About window to PAW and cleaned up the delete and delete
          to EOL bugs.
       Fixed the CC bugs for getting the first and last call.
       Released: 20-Nov-93

0.13   A biggie!  Changed the user files to one single user file.  The
          users directory is still created for data but there is no
          'Pipeline.dat' file anymore.  The UserData.idx is doubly linked
          for alphabetical sorting and can be optimised with 'Rebuild'.
       Added InitUserKey, NextUserKey and EndUserKey to the library for
          traversing the user list.  Alpha/Chrono Forward/Reverse modes are
          all supported and have been tested.
       CHECKALIAS added to Rexx.  Returns non-NULL if the given name is
          already being used.
       Added INITUSERKEY, NEXTUSERKEY, ENDUSERKEY, GETKEYNAME and
          GETKEYALIAS to Rexx commands to allow user list traversing in
          scripts.
       Did some more on the user editor.  The new (smaller) GUI is now
          being used and it interfaces with PL to load the users.
       Made ParDoor more PL aware when returning the menu set type and also
          added the code so the door can change the user data.
       Added a semaphore into the library so no-one will read while the
          structure is being updated.
       Added USERFROMKEY to Rexx.  Works like LOADUSER but you supply a key
          which was got from INITUSERKEY or NEXTUSERKEY commands.
       Finally added some flags to the WRITE command in Rexx.  NOMORE,
          ISMENU and NOBREAK are supported now.
       Added DeleteUser to the library but other routines need to be
          adjusted for it to be usable.
       IMPORTANT - Rewrote the NextRexxArg function for C style control
          characters.  I.e instead of putting '*n' for a return you now put
          '\n'.
       Released: 25-Nov-93

0.14   Finally re-wrote the library and rexx command docs.
       Wrote Connector for people who don't have a mailer.  Answers and
          connects users auto-magically.
       Wrote the first install script.
       Fixed a few Enforcer hits.  Still two about somewhere but they're
          only byte reads from location zero.  I'll fix them ASAP.
       Removed ANSWER and HANGUP from the Rexx commands.  Either the mailer
          or Connector handles all this now.
       Added small window for Pipeline if it can't open the APPIcon.  A
          menu is attached with a quit option.
       General tidy up of everything!
       Pipeline enters the exciting beta test stage as Lars joins the
          club :)
       Released: 27-Nov-93

0.15   Reworked GetChar() a bit to get it TOTALLY sorted.
       Added MenuRead to Rexx.
       Added GetHotChar to Library.
       Removed line process code into a separate program.
       Moved Rexx Server code into main Pipeline code.
       General re-write of lots of functions.
       Added several fields to the SharedData.
       Fixed last two Enforcer hits.
       Rewrote all routines to do with User handling.  PL now builds it's
          own index arrays in memory when loading.  This means that user
          list searching is now almost instant.
       Got rid of USER:UserData.idx.
       Wrote the System Usage graph program (hurrah!).
       DeleteUser now works.
       Rewrote the user file rebuilder.
       More cleaning up and fixing of various routines.
       Released: 18-Dec-93

0.16   Wrote the Computer types editor and the library code bits to with it.
       Merged MENUREAD and READ for more flexability.
       Added a few new control codes.
       Reduced CPU usage for local lines.
       PL now flushes the log file after a users call.
       PL is now more time aware!
       Cleaned up SysUsage a bit.
       BBSLine doesn't allow requesters anymore (fergot..)
       Speeded up user access time and new user handling.
       Fixed bug in CLIDoor/PLShell where 'Press Return' prompts would
          cause the system to freeze up.
       Cleaned up the user editor.
       General cleanup of CLIDoor/PLShell with some new options.
       Cleaned up XPR_PL - Now shows the protocol name and works fine if it
          can't lock the watcher screen.  The window appears if the watcher
          screen is opened during a transfer.
       Improved PAW - no more invisible text on 1-2 bitplanes.  Reqtools
          requesters open on screen but all other requesters are disabled.
       Released: 19-Jan-94

0.17   Added all the library routines to add gadgets to the control screen.
       Changed CONTROL to support the new gadget stuff.
       Added Iconify to PAW.
       Wrote ChatStatus.
       Changed the user editor to non-font-adaptive mode (the gadgets
          messed up otherwise).
       Fixed CHECKALIAS.
       Added EXPANDCC to Rexx.
       ExpandCC will no longer crash if you forget the delimiter.
       Added a few new messages to the status window.
       Wrote the line status watcher (LSW).
       Added Iconify to UserEditor.
       Updated docs!
       Released: 24-Jan-94

0.18   PL doesn't throw a fit anymore if it cannot find the pipeline.library.
       Much faster searching on user names.
       Made 'DoorControl' pure and cleaner.
       Got rid of the 'NewShell Process xx' messages whenever CLIDOORs are
          run.
       Really got stuck into PSL (Pipeline Script Language).  Finally got
          the code right for priority based arithmatic!  The rest should be
          fairly easy now.
       Fixed problem with starting doors with no arguments.
       Removed all hard coded paths in 'Pipeline' and 'pipeline.library'.
          All paths are now defined using the 'Prefs/System' program.
       Updated the user editor to use the new paths.
       PAW now clones the workbench screen if it can't load it's config.
       Released: 16-Feb-94

0.19   Revamped the chat routines so StartChat() doesn't block.
       Added palette to PAW.
       Released: 16-Feb-94

0.32   Added Language support with hi-8 bit character translation support!
       Added Language windows to Prefs/System.
       All config files now in Pipeline:Config/
       Changed XPR_PL - should reset the serial to the state it found it in.
       Changed SharedData and added a couple of fields to the line
          structure.
       Started the Pipeline TCP/IP Internet interface.
       Added scalable font support to RIP routines.
       DETECTANSI & DETECTRIP rexx commands done.
       Fixed enforcer hit in BBSLine.
       Fixed serial problems.
0.42   DISPLAY now uses 'More? Yes/No' prompts instead of 'Press return'.
0.46   Added CALLSCRIPT to Rexx commands.
0.49   Fixed DOESUSEREXIST.
       Updated Rexx/Lib docs.
       Added iconify to Control and rearranged menus.
       Released: 14-Mar-94

0.59   Fixed the bug in CLIDoor which caused the WaitReturn to be
          unbreakable.
       Added CLEAR parameter to WAITRETURN in Rexx.
       Released: 15-Mar-94

0.70   Speeded up sorting of UserIdx's a lot.
       Fixed XPR_PL and added some logging.
       Added logging to StartPL and Connector.
       Released: 16-Mar-94

0.71   Added LastCaller nodes to shared data.
       Added ONLINE to Rexx.
       Fixed a couple of bugs in ParDoor.
0.73   Completely rewrote PAW.  Now has nice GUI when user not online.
       Added version fields to SharedData.
       WriteLine now returns information.
0.78   PAW now at v0.138 and is just about complete.
       Chat will not start if there is no user online.
       Released: 19-Mar-94

0.114  Implemented IEMSI support.
       Added STARTIEMSI and DETECTIEMSI to Rexx.
0.136  Added GETIEMSIINFO and SETIEMSIOpts to Rexx.
       Updated library/rexx docs.
       Fixed StartPL!
       Added IEMSI info to System.cfg.
       IEMSI seems to work ok.
       Released: 23-Mar-94

0.173  Temporary lack of interest in the history file ;)
       Custom Pipe system implemented - replaces the fifo.library by good
          ol' Matt Dillon.  Finally puts the PIPEs into Pipeline...
       Door Handler written - Various doors that weren't working with the
          fifo-handler now work.
       fifo.library/fifo-handler are now not needed at all by the Pipeline
          system.
       Found a bug in DETECTANSI and DETECTRIP.
       Various improvements and speed ups etc.
       DETECTRIP now works but terminal needs to support RIPscrip v1.54.
       Added RIPONLY and TXTONLY flags to WRITE command.
       Finally fixed the bug in XprXfer which caused the text to be garbled
          after a Zmodem download.
0.188  Wrote the BiXfer program.  Uses the slightly altered xpr specs.
       Implemented User Booting!
       Wrote BootUser to kill users from CronTabs and the like.
       Added the needed code into XprXfer for upload.
       Implemented User event logs.
       Added CHKUSERSTATS and SHOWEVENTS to Rexx.
       Fixed Time() function in library.  Much faster replacement for SAS
          version and can be used safely from rexx funcs/assembler progs.
       Pipeline will now boot users off if they run out of time.
Released 18-May-94

0.191  Finished the new and improved Connector.  Now has a nice GUI and
          even it's very own ARexx port and command set!
       Removed the chat messages from Pipeline.
       New type of chat char - TYPE_START.  Sent to a chat routine before
          any keys are pressed.  Allows the chat to setup the screen etc.
       DeleteUser now deletes the user directory and all the contents
          thereof.
       Added LineOutputMode() to library.
       Added CC's 150-154 for controlling output.
       Added CC 175 for showing contents of ENV variables.
       Added Inactive timer.  Now boots user off if they don't type
          anything for 'x' seconds.  'x' is defined in Prefs/System
          program.
Released 23-May-94

0.207  Serious bug finding/squelching session!
       Fixed nasty bug in CLIDOOR which would cause a hang when waiting for
          return key (during user lister mainly).
       Fixed problems with LoadUser which caused spurious data to be loaded
          sometimes.
       Fixed problems with WriteLine where data sometimes didn't get fully
          written (most noticably in Space Empire!)
       Moved PAW key config to a separate file which all running PAW's
          share.  When the keys are changed in one PAW, all PAW's are
          affected.
       Added ClipBoard pasting support to PAW.  Usual Amiga-V thing.
          ClipBoard cutting cannot be supported because of the custom ANSI
          routines...
       Wrote example util called 'Logger'.  Saves all output of a line to a
          file.
       Fixed divide by zero bug in PAW.
       Added lots of new control codes.
       Changed some control codes around, see docs.
       FINALLY fixed problem when running Hack & Slash which would hang the
          line.
       PAW now has ASL font requester.
       Serious clean up of Rexx code.
       Fixed small bug in the input routines.
       Implemented timeouts on Reading.  Only accessable by using the Rexx
          READ command for now.
       Added Save parameter to SendLineMsg command.
Released: 26-May-94

0.222  Fixed bug in PAW when selecting font for the first time.
       PAW wouldn't actually do 16 colours properly!  (Probably a bug from
          the re-write).  Fixed anyhow!
       Cleaned up and fixed ParDoor.
Released: 27-May-94

0.231  Fixed handling of WAIT_CHAR packet in door handler.  Now Citadel
          Space Empire works a treat ;)
       Cleaned up UserRebuild, removed hard-coded USER: path (now needs to
          be run in the user directory).  Also, if PL is active, it
          rebuilds the internal user indexes too!
Released: 27-May-94

0.234  Removed console.device from PAW.  Should hopefully fix some
          problems.
       Added cursor ghosting to PAW when window is active/inactive.
       Added user data to title bar and new menu command to allow cycling
          through the various bits.
       Just about finished of the Intenet Mail Processor.  Now does dupe
          checking, reply linking and exporting.
       Had a real good go at trying to fix all of PAW's font/screen/ANSI
          problems.  Lots of stuff fixed!
Released: 31-May-94

0.240  PAW now stretches it's GUI to fill the screen.
       Totally fixed PAW's ANSI editing bits.
       Updated Pipeline's ANSI editing.  See CLE.doc.
Released: 31-May-94

0.246  Fixed small bug in ANSI editing routines.
       Added ANSI editing routines to library.
       CLIDoors now use new ANSI editing routines.
       Added TERMCAPS to Rexx.
       Added more support for RIP in DisplayFile, OpenTextFile and DISPLAY.
       New user flag - UF_WANTRIP.
0.254  Pipeline now detects ANSI and RIP in a local logon.
       Found small bug in PAW which would leave the screen open when
          exiting.
0.262  Fixed small bug at logon when sometimes the first letter would be
          appended to the end because of IEMSI detection.
       Added OwnDevUnit.library support to Connector.
       Fixed enforcer hits caused by EXPANDCC being used on lines which
          have no scripts.
       Fixed font related problems in Control.
       Added AddPipeSignal & RemPipeSignal to library - private functions
          (for now) but they mean that all pipeline.library I/O functions
          (DisplayFile, ReadLine, etc) can be used safely from within
          CLIDoors.
       Added all Bulletin functions.
       Added DISPLAYBLTN, LISTBLTNS, UNREADBLTNS to rexx.
       Wrote Bulletin Manager CLI program.
       Fixed Time() and GMTime()
       Wrote the Bulletin Editor - Real time GUI experience 8-)
       Wrote BM.doc and BulletinEd.doc
Released: 16-Jun-94

0.296  Updated/Fixed Chat routines.
Released: 16-Jun-94

0.308  Implemented Pipeline Doors with their own set of I/O routines.
       New Rexx command: PLDOOR.
       New library functions: ReadLineTagList, GetYesNo and (with new
          linker library) ReadLineTags and LPuts.
       Implemented global menu commands.  New library functions: LoadGCmds,
          UnLoadGCmds, FindGCmd and FreeGCmd.
       Wrote 'ReloadGCmds' program for updating global commands while PL is
          running.
       New Rexx command: GETGLOBALCMD.
       UserList, ParDoor and XlkDoor converted to Pipeline doors.
       Fixed some bugs!
       New library routine: ErrorLogWrite.
Released: 22-Jun-94

0.310  Fixed guru in PAW if you had 2+ nodes online and you iconified one of
          them.
       Fixed bug in PL which reused a timer request on startup and exit.
       Fixed GMTime (about time too...)
       Fixed Enforcer and IOTorture in Connector.
       Added ANSI Music to PAW :)
       Fixed small bug in PAW with Amiga ANSI sequences.
       Wrote lots of RIP code.
       Fixed THE BUG!!!  Twas in DoorControl and made running PL on a 68000
          system real hell.  Looking really stable now though...
       Added the watcher functions into the library so they can all talk to
          each other(!)
       Wrote a quick ARexx 'graffiti door' script.
       Fixed enforcer in XprXfer and reworked a couple of functions.
       Fixed problems with callers sending CR/LF instead of just CR.
0.332  Fixed foolish bug in SHOWEVENTS.
       Wrote 'WhosOnline' and 'SendNodeMsg' scripts.
       Moved RESETTIMER code into ONLINE as there wasn't much point having
          them as separate functions.
       BBSLine now writes to the PLError.log with any script problems.
          Also logs the official Rexx error msgs!
0.340  Fixed hackable things!
       Wrote Hydra protocol.
       Fixed possible user bugs.
       INITLINE now updates users number of calls.
       Fixed bugs in Hydra.
       Moved Clipboard paste & ANSI music routines to library and RIP now
          uses them.
       Wrote menu editor for Control.
       Control now has support for IFF backdrops.
0.356  Fixed bugs in SignalWatchers function.
       Wrote spammy new installer script.
Released: 31-Aug-94

0.361  Messed about with the PAW screen a bit.  Rewrote the graph routines
          and they are now mighty smart.
       Fixed various bugs.  Things are working just fine.
       Fixed command line bug in Connector.
       Fixed IFF decode problem in Control.
Released: 04-Sep-94

0.361  PAW now uses icon system.  Make sure you copy the supplied PAW.info
          icon to Pipeline:Config/Icons.
       XprXfer now uses Watcher system so it knows when to iconify.
          Pressing the close gadget now works a lot faster too.
       XprXfer now remebers the data when it iconifies so when the window
          re-appears the data does too.
       XprXfer window sorted out (was too small).
       FreeWatcher now frees all pending messages to stop system hangs.
       The LastCaller structure now includes a copy of the user structure
          as it was when the user logged off.  There is also a semaphore in
          the SharedData which should be obtained when looking at the list.
Released: 04-Sep-94

0.364  Lots more done to XprXfer.  Even has two bars showing a percentage
          of batch and file done.  Just about finished now.  Lots of minor
          bug fixes.
       Re-worked the Bulletin Editor.  Allows you to edit access levels and
          adjust the order of the bulletins.  Feels a lot nicer to use now.
       Minor bug fixes to a few rexx functions.
       ASYNCREXX added to rexx.
       Updated rexx docs (and partially did library docs).
0.366  Wrote some general purpose node manipulation macros (nodes.h) to
          replace the link lib I was using.  (Nick - use these, their fab
          :-) )
       The user system now only needs to re-sort the entire user list when
          you get twenty new users in a session.  (This number will be
          configurable).  Doesn't actually take much time anyway...
       Deleting users is now a case of setting a flag in the users flags
          field (but don't do this yourself - call DeleteUser as it does
          some other internal stuff).  This means you will be able to
          UnDelete Users.
       UserRebuild now deletes the users directory and all files contained
          within.
Released: 07-Sep-94

0.367  Fixed minor bug in DeleteUser.
       Gadgets added to the control screen now have their text set
          correctly to the screens font and Control takes note of this
          while laying gadgets out.
       MenuEditor is now font adaptive.
       Control now gives more options for it's public screen.  You can set
          it to be the default screen, to shanghai windows, and to pop to
          front when a window opens on it.
Released: 07-Sep-94

0.380  Implemented new language system.
       The text config part has gone from the System.cfg as there are now
          #?.lang files stored in Pipeline:Config/Language which define
          each language.
       New library functions: LoadLanguage, Freelanguage, GetLangStr,
          ReLoadLanguage, LoadLangExtra, FreeLangExtra.
       New Rexx functions: PROMPT, GETLANGSTR
       New library functions: LLVPrintf, ELVPrintf, LVPrintf (for formatted
          printing)
       New routines in pl.lib: LLPrintf, ELPrintf, LPrintf.
Released: 08-Sep-94

0.399  Added lots of new error checking messages to PL during loading the
          System.cfg.
       Added lots more error msgs to the library when loading languages.
          Errors are written to PLError.log.
Released: 09-Sep-94

0.419  Modernised ExpandCC and added ExpandCCStr in library.
       PAW and BBSLine now lock Pipeline on startup (was causing some 68000
          hangs on exit).
       LISTBLTNS now back in rexx.  Uses languages!
       Improved the speed and regularity of the pipes a bit.
       Fixed IEMSI a bit.
       Prefs/System now uses ASL instead of ReqTools and my own (pretty)
          getfile button.
       Added MenuSet window to System config.
       Re-wrote DisplayFile and OpenTextFile in the library.
       Added dupe checking function to UserManager.
       NICENAME (rexx) now calls NiceLine automatically.
0.423  Implemented text file buffering in library.
       Fixed many bugs in the RIP ANSI routines.
       ParDoor is now more intelligent when displaying files.
       DisplayFile/DISPLAY do not try language or menuset extensions if
          none have been defined.
       No more 'More?' prompts in RIP files.
       Wrote 'TextPreLoad' for preloading/flushing text files.
       If user has RIP enabled, PL will set an ANSI palette before showing
          ANSI files and starting doors.
       RIP can now be put into NTSC mode if you supply 'NTSC' on the
          command line.
0.440  Removed time/date string for events shown with SHOWEVENTS.
       Wrote CLI program 'SendMsg' to send messages to lines from CronTabs
          etc.
       Menu Sets fully implemented in PL/Rexx/Library/System.
       New Rexx command: SETMSFLAGS
       Connector and StartPL now use GetConnectMode() and store the flags
          in the line structure.
       BootUser will no longer kick lines with no users on them.
       Fixed some more bugs in RIP.
       RIP now takes more arguments.  NTSC forces screen into 50Hz mode (if
          you have ECS+ chips).  DEPTH <1-4> allows you to set the RIP
          screen depth.  Setting a number less than 4 will automatically
          turn on NOFILL mode.
Released: 24-Sep-94

0.450  New flag for DISPLAY, PLDOOR and CLIDOOR: NORESET.  Stops the RIP
          terminal reset codes from being displayed.
       Implemented new circle/arc/pie drawing system into RIP.  Now much
          faster.
       RIP_ARC, RIP_PIE_SLICE, RIP_OVAL_PIE_SLICE implemented in RIP.
       Made RIP work properly with RIPslide ;)
0.475  Added More? Y/N/C into Display.
       If RIP terminal has been detected but the user doesn't want RIP then
          their screen is reset during PUTONLINE.
       Added Banned User support into Prefs/System PL and Rexx.
       Extra args for CLRSCR, PLDOOR and CLIDOOR.
       Changed CHKUSERSTATS a bit.
       System.cfg is now loaded through the library which will make
          updating nice and easy.
       PL now resets the ANSI colours after a WaitReturn etc prompt.
       Fixed small bug in PAW's ANSI.
Released: 07-Oct-94

0.476  Fixed serious serial bugs in BBSLine and PL.
       Fixed Connectors output window to handle long strings.
Released: 09-Oct-94

0.494  Last calls are now saved to disk and reloaded when PL starts up.
       PAW now displays the log on/off times in 24 hour format.
       Fixed XprXfer's strange log messages.
       Transfer bars now update every 1% in XprXfer.
       Fixed bug where users with ANSI turned off still got the colour
          'More? Y/N' prompts!
       PL now remembers the current colour settings throughout the session
          so there should be no more text files that change colour after a
          'More?' prompt.
       Optimized BBSLine's rexx message handling a tiny bit.
       Most rexx user functions dealing with getting/setting data can now
          operate on users not currently online.
       Wrote UseNet news library and PostNews/Processor progs.
       LOTS of other small bug fixes/enhancements!  Getting bored writing
          them all down in here ;)
Released: 01-Nov-94

0.515  Added Access stuff into LineEditor - you can now set when users can
          logon or impose restrictions on baud and access levels for
          certain times of day.
       Added CHKLINEACCESS and SETACCLIMIT to Rexx.
Released: 08-Nov-94

0.520  Wrote a whole new logon script with IEMSI, banned users and event
          support.
       Added USERCREDIT to REXX.
       PL is now aware of screen positioning codes so more prompts don't
          appear when they shouldn't. (NL)
       Fixed bug where more prompts would come up one line to early.
       Fixed bug in PAW with weird colours on the data screen. (KG)
       Speeded up XlkDoor when doing 'MayGetChar'
Released: 12-Nov-94

0.521  CLIDoor now returns the result code of the door it runs.
       Fixed bug in NiceLine which would overwrite one byte of memory if
          the line began with a semi-colon.
       OOps!  After a call, PAW would set the draw mode to JAM1 instead of
          JAM2 causing text to be or'd onto the screen.
       Resident PLDoors are now supported.
       BBSLine was opening serial device even when told not to. (BC)
0.524  Removed hard coded 'More?' strings.  You now need to add it to your
          Language config file(s).
       RIPs screen is now public.
       PAW's public screen name is now 'ANSI.x' (x is the line number) and
          RIPs one is 'RIP.x'.  You don't have to search for both though:
          use the new library function 'LockWatcherScreen'.
       XprXfer can now open on the RIP screen.
       Users data now appears on the RIP title bar.
0.525  New watcher message WM_USERON sent when a user is put online.
Released: 17-Nov-94

0.527  PL no longer processes the Rexx msgs itself: they get passed directly
          to the line process.  This has speeded up operation a bit.
       Computers prefs program is now not needed as it has been incorperated
          into the System prog.
       Fixed bug in XprXfer where it wouldn't run if it couldn't lock a
          screen (NL).
       Connector now uses the icon system and has a nice new icon.
       SENDLINEMSG will now accept '*' for a line number (to send the
          message to all lines).
       GetGad() was setting the hit box of the gadgets one pixel too high.
       SendLineMsg() now works when a user hasn't yet been putonline (NL).
       FakeXfer fixed.
       BootUser also now works when a user hasn't yet been putonline.
Released: 21-Nov-94

0.531  Fixed bug in PLSHELL where remote user had to press return before it
          would run.
       PL now shuts down nice and quick.
       Added some new functions in the library for storing extra data about
          each user.
0.548  DoorHandler can now work with progs who try to open '*' as thier
          output filehandle.
       Fixed rare Enforcer hit in DoorHandler.
       PL now ALWAYS puts a null char after a '+' char to prevent putting
          your modem into cmd mode.
0.551  New Rexx functions for controlling user extra data - see docs.
Released: 26-Nov-94

0.554  Fixed bugs in the editing routines.  Added ^O & ^P for jumping
          between words.
       Rewrote most of the UseNet news stuff.
       Lots of mini-bugs fixed...  Clean up of code.
       CC 251 added.
       Started work on the mail processor.
Released: 05-12-94

0.582  Fixed problems with CR/LF pairs in menus.
       Rewrote Bin/PostImport for speed.
       Added new field to SysVars - sv_Flags.
       You can now specify whether local calls will be added to the total
          calls field in the saved data. (IF)
       Import almost done in mail processor.
       Wrote fake dlg.library and DLGDoor.
       StartPL now only switches to real baud if there is no '/ARQ' in the
          connect string and DCF_FLOATBAUD has been enabled.
       SETUSERDATA now truncates strings if they are too long for the
          dest field. (PB)
       MakeNewUser() now truncates user names longer than 30 chars because
          of AmigaDOS restriction on file name lengths.  Aliases remain at
          40 chars however. (PB)
       Added lots of new options to CLIDOOR for controlling how ^C & ^D
          work.
       Improved DLGDoor.  Now writes a fake User.Data and t:TRx.port.
       Fixed bug in PAW/RIP in function key routines where %s was still
          being expanded to WATCHER.x
       Fixed small bug in PAW's ANSI.
       PAW, RIP & Control now use newlook menus for WB3.
Released: 23-Dec-94

Have a Zeusy Christmas, I'm off to Sheffield...

0.590  The users Event.log wasn't being deleted!
       Prefs/System now has lots of error messages in.
       Fixed small bug in mbuunews.library.
       The number of last calls in list now relates to each node and not
          affect the global number.
       Fixed probs with GetCType and CC 69.
       Fixed lots of probs with TextPreLoad.  You can now flush the text
          files in memory if Zeus isn't running.
       Another small bug in PAW's ANSI!
Released: 31-Dec-94

0.593  Added some more bits into the fake xenolink.library.
       Fixed potentially dangerous bug in XlkDoor.
Released: 31-Dec-94

1995 and Zeus enters it's 3rd year of development!

0.593  Fixed iconify probs with PAW/RIP.  If you started PAW in iconify
          mode, then opened the screen and iconified again, it would
          re-open when a user logged off!
       More stuff put into the XlkDoor and fake xenolink.library.
Released: 04-Jan-95

0.597  Fixed bug with CC 103 (IF)
       Fixed bug in LoadUserXData (NL)
       Fixed bug in ErrorLogWrite (NL)
       You can now stack commands in the Control menus by using a semi
          colon between each cmd. (MB)
       New menu entry in Control - 'Reload Menus' (MB)
       Lots of error messages in Control.
       Control now gets it's icon from Zeus:Config/Icons/
       Fixed various Prefs progs so they open on the Control screen.
       LineEditor doesn't use reqtools any more.
       Fixed small bug in my GetFile gadget.
       Once a backdrop picture has been loaded into Control, you can edit
          the palette and it'll STAY edited!  (MB)
       Fixed Enforcer in LineEditor.
       Removed the modem types part from LineEditor.
       Fixed plenty of code in MenuEditor.
       May have found a bug in the Xlk emulation which may make it work for
          those testers who've been having probs.
Released: 08-Jan-95

0.623  CLIDoors/PLShell do not allow expanding of control codes anymore
          unless you specify it.
       Added command line history to editing routines.  PLShell is the only
          thing which takes advantage of this so far...
       Zeus wasn't stripping out Amiga CSI codes if the user didn't want
          ANSI codes.  This has been fixed and also, Amiga CSI codes are
          translated to IBM ones.
       Chat now strips out incoming ANSI codes and the delete key.
       Import is finished in ZMP.
Released: 10-Jan-95

0.624  Fixed up ConW.  Now has definable window pos/size/font and you can 
          choose which screen it opens on.
       Did some work on DTE, much better ^C detection and you now use ^Z to
          save & quit and ^A to abort.
       New Rexx command - CHECKINPUT.  Returns 5 if the user has typed
          something, 0 otherwise.
       Fixed a bug in SaveUser() to do with the XData. (NL)
Released: 15-Jan-95

0.628  Did some work on Connector.  Is now font adaptive and everything
          works!
       DETECTIEMSI did not handle loss of carrier.
       Prefs/Progs and Prefs/Internet were not opening their file
          requesters on the PIPELINE screen.
0.665  Added new rexx command ABBEREXX which allows you to run rexx scripts
          in an Abberexx environment.
Released: 18-Jan-95

0.683  Wrote my favourite library function!  SearchArray().  Uses a quick
          search algorithm and can handle any sized elements!
       WRITE, READ, DISPLAY, CLIDOOR, GETIEMSIINFO, GET/SETUSERDATA,
          GET/SET/CLRUSERFLAG and ABBEREXX now all use SearchArray() to
          speed up argument processing.
       DISPLAY now returns the same error codes as WRITE.
       Finally fixed the bug with users number of calls being incremented
          too much. (IF)
Released: 22-Jan-95

0.685  Did lots of work on HydraXfer.  Now has a smaller info window, and
          two chat windows (remote and local).  Can now work when PAW is
          iconified and supports the watcher system so it will (un)iconify
          when PAW/RIP does.
Released: 25-Jan-95

0.688  Updated the ChatWrite routine.  +++ no longer breaks the modem! (MB)
       Changed QUITPL to QUITZEUS.
       Added aliases for PLDOOR -> ZDOOR and PLSHELL -> ZSHELL.  The
          originals will still work for now.
       You can now quit Zeus by doing CLI> rx "address 'ZEUS' 'QUITZEUS'"
       Fixed minor Enforcers in BBSLine when closing down (Hadn't shown up
          before!)
Released: 26-Jan-95

0.711  Finally implemented asynchronos ARexx commands in Zeus!  The new
          system is backwards compatible so it won't cause any probs.
       Fixed bug in Chat routines from 0.688 where it filtered out ANSI
          codes!
       Took over the mbpipeline and mbstarmsg libraries.
       Speeded up mbpipeline quite a bit in preparation for finishing the
          mail processor.
Released: 29-Jan-95

0.712  If a file is passed to FileXfer which has 'LOCK' as it's file
          comment (case sensitive), it will not be sent. (IF)
       Fixed highly stupid bug in XprXfer where only every alternate file
          was sent!!!
       WRITE and DISPLAY now return 2 if the user answered 'C' to a More
          Y/N/C prompt, 1 if everything was displayed and <0 if there was
          an error or the user broke the output.
       Rewrote some of mbstarmsg.library so it doesn't use the StarMsgCfg
          config anymore.  Instead, it auto detects Foozle messages but
          always saves in standard Fido format.
       When using the LM_NOFIDOINFO flag with the mbpl or mbsm they strip
          out tear and origin lines as well as seenby's and path's.
Released: 30-Jan-95

0.722  New library routine: ZLoadSeg() which not only scans the segment
          list (for resident programs) but also passes through all the
          current path dirs looking for the program.
       Completely revamped the way Zeus starts and runs CLIDOORs.
       Fixed carrier checking in ParDoor, added a VERY simple editor and
          fixed a couple of other minor bugs.
       Completed export in the mail processor.
0.763  Fixed two enforcers in ZMP.
       Wrote ZIMP (Zeus Internet Mail Processor).
       Renamed ZNP (Zeus News Processor) to ZUMP (Zeus Usenet News
          Processor).
       Fixed some stuff in RIP.
       Fixed a couple of things in ZMP.  Now works from both point and node
          setups.
Released: 15-Feb-95

0.763  Added logging and lots of error reporting to ZMP.
       ZMP now handles packet level passwords and crash mail.
       Fixed missing tear line in mbstarmsg (NL).
       mbuunews, mbstarmsg and mbpipeline now support the LM_NOTEXT flag.
Released: 15-Feb-95

0.763  ZMP can now pack/unpack packets in a temporary directory.
       ZMP can now store attached files in a separate directory.
       Fixed problem with 3d seen-by's and path lines. (AB)
       Tidied up ZMP's CLI/Log output a bit.
       Fixed ZMP address parsing bug (KG)
Released: 17-Feb-95

0.764  Made mbpipeline append a \r to a messages origin line if one doesn't
          exist already.
       Switch ZMP history to a separate doc.
       Added ICONIFY and UNICONIFY to Rexx. (MB)
       Fixed small bug in MakeNewUser.
       Fixed bugs in control gadget library functions.
       Control can now open it's own screen (as it has been doing) or open
          a window on the workbench screen.
       Control should now be able to handle a screen with up to eight
          bitplanes (256 colours).
       Moved watcher function key processing into the library.
       Watcher function keys can now contain all normal Zeus control codes.
       You can now have a watcher function key dump a text file to the
          line.  Set the key type to 'Text' and the key data to
          '<Path:Filename'.
Released: 21-Feb-95

0.770  Moved all the user routines out of the pipeline.library and into a
          separate userbase.library.  I am working on two versions of this
          lib.  One is uses lots of memory and is fast (current routines)
          and the other stores everything on disk.
       Minor fixes in ZLoadSeg()
       Played about with DoorControl a bit :)
       Fixed the foolish menu bug in Control.
Released: 24-Feb-95

0.770  Fixed a possible divide by zero in XprXfer.
       Improved the post xfer file processing slightly.
       Fixed up ZeusUpdate.rexx - now creates the directory structure so
          it should work a lot better!
Released: 26-Feb-95

0.770  ZeusUpdate.rexx doesn't copy updated files with a filelength of
          zero (i.e. the update didn't work) and also generates a log file.
Released: 28-Feb-95

0.770  Reduced memory usage in Control.
       Fixed problem with gadgets on the Control screen not disappearing.
       Wrote a new userbase.library which uses much less memory than the
          existing one and is still pretty speedy.
       Fixed (semi) bug in BBSLine where return codes from scripts that
          were higher than zero produced an 'Undiagnosed internal error'
          line in PLError.log (GetFile.pl being the example).
       Wrote a new message base library 'mbzeus.library'.  This basically
          replaces mbpipeline as it's faster and has some nice new features
          like self-optimising files(!).
       Expanded the mb specs adding Update, Rescan, Maintenance and Trim
          routines.
       Wrote mbManager to take advantage of these new functions.  Detects
          if a mb lib handles the new extensions.
       Added CHECKABORT rexx function.
Released: 4-Mar-95

0.773  Fixed a bug in mbzeus when loading a message with NOTEXT (NL)
       mbzeus was swapping the Date and ArriveDate fields.
Released: 5-Mar-95

0.809  Changed UF_NOANSI to UF_ANSICOLR and added UF_ANSIPOS and
          UF_ANSICOMP user flags.
       Cut the serial opening code from BBSLine which wasn't really needed
          and caused problems anyhow.
       Implemented ANSI compression and re-wrote Zeus' main output function.
       Fixed a couple of things in mbzeus and added new mb* func:
          mbScanMsgHdrs().
       Added lots of new commands into the library to replace the current
          Next(Rexx|Async)Arg and Reply(Async)Function.
       All the async commands I want to support are now operational.
       Re-wrote all the main output functions AGAIN!  Now handles split
          ANSI and Control codes.  ANSI doors can now be run with colour
          disabled.

       The long, slow task of renaming everything from Pipeline to Zeus
          begins today!  See the file 'EverythingMustGo.doc' for details.

       Wrote ZPatch which patches OpenLibrary and LockPubScreen so every
          thing still works!
       Added rescan to mbzeus.  Updates the High/Low/HSBN pointers in an
          area.
       Re-Wrote ZPatch in assembler since C wasn't quite transparent
          enough and caused Enforcer hits.  Source included.
       Added new Rexx command 'LASTINPUT' for detecting whether the data
          from the last READ came from local (RC=0) or remote (RC=5).
Released: 20-Mar-95

0.856  Fixed small bug in CHKLINEACCESS.
       Re-worked GetConnectMode().  Now works if the 'CONNECT' part is
          missing.
       CHKUSERSTATS was shagged!
       Fixed hotkey bug.
       Zeus is now more tolerant of CC's which miss the '|'
       Fixed some nice Enforcers in HydraXfer. (KP)
Released: 31-Mar-95

0.867  Fixed Enforcer in XprXfer (KP)
       Added InitArea function to mbzeus and mbManager (AB)
       UserManager now checks for zero length user names during a rebuild. (AB)
       Added new rexx funcs: SCREENTOFRONT and SCREENTOBACK which switch
          the lines watcher screen to front/back.
       LoadUser() and LoadUserFromKey() now check if a user is deleted if
          their record is held in the memory list.
       MakeNewUser() checks for duplicate names.
       ubFindUserIdx() checks for deleted users.
       Added lots of error reporting into userbase.library
Released: 6-Apr-95

0.889  Fixed bug in XprXfer which stopped multiple uploads - Soz!  (Many...)
       Fixed Enforcer in SearchArray()
       Fixed IEMSI stuff and added some more logging. (KP,AB)
       Fixed bad error reports from mbzeus. (AB)
Released: 10-Apr-95

0.889  Fixed a couple of minor bugs in zeus.library
       ErrorLogWrite() *was* opening PLError.log - Sorry Tony!  :)  (AB)
       Improved command stacking slightly.  Now strips leading spaces
          and semi-colons.
       Fixed a couple of things in mbzeus.  Also added LOTS more error
          reporting in Load/Save message as well as maint functions.
       Speeded up message loading in mbzeus a bit.
Released: 18-Apr-95

0.891  Zeus/BBSLine now use the extensions used in the text system when
          looking for rexx scripts.  .pl is still supported for now but
          the official extension is now .zeus
       mbzeus' maintenance function is now more thorough!  Goes through
          the header file and renumbers the messages to fix any weird
          ZMP crash bugs.
       Fixed the bad return code from mbInitialise in mbzeus (NL)
Released: 20-Apr-95

0.894  Added new break mode to CLIDoor - EOFBREAK.  When Zeus wants to
          make the door quit, it closes the pipes thus making Read()
          return NULL.  If this doesn't work then no doors can be run
          on that line, however...
       Fixed up how Zeus quits doors a bit.  DeepSpace now quits fine if
          you use the PASSC option on the CLIDoor line.
       Cleaned up most of mbzeus' functions and reduced the code size by
          re-using my error messages :)
       mbzeus' maintenance now renumbers the messages from the original
          low pointer.
       When doing a maint with mbManager/mbzeus, you should do a rescan
          first to correct any low pointer problems.
       mbzeus' maintenance also strips out deleted messages.
       Added new option to CLIDoor - NOSERIAL.  Runs the door as normal
          but input and output is only possible via local.  Designed to
          run doors which take over the serial port.
       Fixed problems with the self optimizing routines in mbzeus.  This
          was causing mbzeus to try and allocate huge amounts of memory
          and is probably to blame for all the probs everyone's been
          having.  Lemme know!
Released: 21-Apr-95

0.899  Fixed infinite loop created when the various 'More?' prompts had
          newlines in them.  I don't recommend putting newlines into those
          prompts since the user will loose data off the top of the screen
          but Zeus won't crash anymore! (MB)
       Forgot to uncomment the code which puts a null char after a '+'!
       Added new option to CALLSCRIPT.  You can now specify the directory
          the script gets started in by specifying 'DIR <Directory>' after
          the script name.
       mbzeus' maintenance functions don't complain if there are no messages
          in the base anymore.  (AB,NL)
       DETECTANSI and DETECTRIP now take an argument which specifies the
          number of 1/10's of a second they will wait before returning
          FALSE.
0.900  Added CC's 157 and 158 to return the lines serial device name and
          unit.
Released: 23-Apr-95

0.901  Fixed bug in Control when going from a window to a screen. (IF)
       Fixed small bug in ANSI's ANSI!
       Fixed order of ANSI's iconify routine.
       Improved (if not fixed) XprXfers buggy percent display.
       Fixed RIP button & icon problems.  (GS)
Released: 26-Apr-95

0.902  RIPs cursor now ghosts when the window goes inactive.
       Fixed problem with RIP buttons not resetting the screen. (GS)
       General cleanup of Watcher iconify/to front/back systems. (AB)
       Some ANSI codes were causing RIP to reference the wrong rastport
          causing wrong colour effects.
Released: 02-May-95

0.904  UserManager REBUILD now checks the length of all string fields
          in the user structures for illegal values. (KP)
Released: 03-May-95

0.904  Added stack field into the MenuEditor.
       MenuEditor can now be used to edit the watcher menus as well!
       Added external menu support into ANSI.
       Ripped lots of code from Control and put it into the library.
       Added external menu support into RIP.
       Fixed small bug in NiceLine() which was causing a character to
          be lost if there was a comment on the same line.  (PB)
Released: 04-May-95

0.905  'Verbosed' up the userbase seek error messages.  Should help find
          whats causing them.  (AB)
       Fixed Control 'Font' ghosting. (SM,NL)
       Fixed bug in GETUSERXDATA.
Released: 13-May-95

0.905  Recompiled mbuunews.library/ZPostNews/ZUNP.  All works again but
          I've decided not to get into gating...
       Even more verbose messages in userbase.library.
       Fixed InitUserScanKey bug when there are no users.  (NL)
       Put some checking in mbzeus so it always loads the correct message.
          If you get an 'Message header misplaced' error then please send
          me your ZeusHdr.x for that area - thanks...
       Fixed another minor bug in GETUSERXDATA! (NL)
Released: 17-May-95

0.909  Made argument passing to scripts a lot easier!
       Played about with the last callers display in ANSI.
       New library command - FileMarkXfer()
       Zeus now breaks the running script when the user is to be booted
          off (through lack of carrier etc).  It only sends one ^C per
          script (unless it's the StartUp or BootUser scripts in which case
          it doesn't send any) so you can catch it using 'signal on break_c'
       Found a use for that unused byte in the user structure!  Now holds
          a code which tells you how the user logged off i.e. 'lost carrier'
          or 'no time left' etc...
       The logs now tell you how the user logged off!  They tried to before
          but they failed ;)
       Zeus was giving users an extra minute online when their time ran
          out!!!
       Added new rexx commands GETALIASFROMNAME, GETNAMEFROMALIAS and
          GETLOGOFFCODE.
       Fixed small bug where users were being added to the last calls list
          without having some of their fields updated first.
0.935  Added new rexx commands SERWRITE and SERREAD. (Docs RSN!)
       Added WRITE substitute - SWRITE.  Doesn't take any flag arguments
          so you don't need to deal with all that tricky quoting!
       FLUSHINPUT wasn't clearing the serial buffer!
Released: 19-May-95

0.937  Fixed a couple of tres nasty bugs in userbase.library.  May well
          stop those seek error messages.
       Whoops!  Broke CHKUSERSTATS in that last update - sorry! (MW)
       INITLINE was getting into an infinite loop sometimes. (MW,NL)
       DETECTANSI and DETECTRIP can now take the optional argument 'FORCE'.
       Added new rexx command 'FORCE8BIT'.
       DTE now accepts high eight bit chars. (KM)
Released: 21-May-95

0.939  mbzeus now saves messages with their numbers reflecting their
          position in the header file.  Should stop the problems with
          finding the wrong messages.
       Stuck the new ANSI flags into Prefs/System -> Menu Sets.
       Fixed semaphore bug in mbuunews.
       Put in ScanMessages and ScanMsgHdrs into mbuunews - cheers Nick :)
       Put in support for optional DSR/Carrier checking (if selected in the
          LineEditor).
       Revamped the chat routines.  You won't notice anything new but it's
          all different!  You can also use WriteLine/ReadLine within
          your chat routine now.
       Put all the Vanilla Key stuff into Prefs/LineEditor and removed
          the OpenDevice flag which isn't used anymore.
       Added TIMEOUT argument to SERREAD.
       Fixed bug in SERREAD when in LINE mode.
       Added support for animated ANSI prompts!
       New user flags (UF_)ANIMPROMPTS and (UF_)ANSIMUSIC.
       WAITRETURN will now show an animated prompt if you define the tag
          'WAITRETURNANIM' in your language file.
       Added ANIM argument to READ.  The arg after it should be the name
          of a tag in your language file which contains an ANIM.
       Added CC's 300 and 301.
Released: 24-May-95

0.970  Fixed MaxCallsPerDay bug. (MW)
       Fixed RIP so it doesn't pop up when ANSI is iconified. (AB)
       Added command line option to Zeus:Bin/Chat.  HOLDTIME will stop
          Zeus taking minutes from the user while they're in chat mode (SR)
       Improved handling of C & D ANSI codes. (NL)
       Zeus takes note of the <CSI>[2J ANSI code. (SM)
       Fixed 'More?' prompts showing up in chat! (RT)
       Fixed white text in chat. (RT)
       Chat now allows high-8 characters. (GS)
       Added CC's 187 & 188. (GS)
       Added AddHistList(), RemHistList() and ClearHistList() to library.
0.1000 Added new rexx command 'SUBTIME <ON|OFF>' which enables/disables
          the users time online decreasing. (PB)
       Added some ReadLineTags tags (RLT_*) to make all options available.
       ReadLineTags/TagList now returns the length of data in the buffer.
       All the input functions now disable ANSI compression while they
          process the users input.  This was causing the delete line code
          not to clear the line properly.
       Fixed probs with ReadLine(). (GS)
Released: 01-Jun-95

0.1008 The system gadgets on the control window now have priority over the
          ones on the window. (PB)
       If Zeus cannot close down properly, it now has a ninety second time
          out (with natty display!) after which it will exit anyway. (RK)
       Fixed some problems BBSLine had with calling BootUser/StartUp. (RK)
       Wrote a new example BootUser.zeus skeleton script showing the use
          of GETLOGOFFCODE.
       Recompiled the Zeus LIB's - only LPuts is left!  All the other
          functions are in the library. (RK)
       Added two character translation tables into the line structure.  One
          for input and t'other for output.
       Zeus now loads a set of character translation configs from
          Zeus:Config/Translation/.
       Added new rexx command 'SETTRANS' for messing about with the
          CharTabs.
       Added 'space' control to Zeus' output function.  If Zeus has to pause
          the output with a 'More?' prompt, you can now press SPACE to bring
          up the next line.  This doesn't work for normal GetYesNo/WaitReturn
          type prompts. (GS)
       Put the code into XprXfer to check if the file already exists but       
          GetFileNoExt() doesn't work ;) (MW)
       Finally sorted IEMSI out!  (Many!)
Released: 09-Jun-95

0.1055 Added new input mode - IR_EOLRET.  Returns -2 if the buffer is filled.
       Animated prompts were not setting the inactivity timeout properly.
       Fixed a couple of problems in mbzeus' scan message routines. (NL)
       Zeus will only apply the char translation tables to data from/to the
          user online. (GS)
       Reversed the order that Zeus writes the data to serial/pipes.  This
          shouldn't be noticable...
       Fixed small bug in userbase.library that might have been causing
          probs with deleting/new users of the same name. (RK)
       Fixed bug when pressing space with WF_USEMOREYN.
       UserManagers REBUILD mode doesn't delete the users directory any more.
          This has been moved to the new DELDIRS mode which deletes all
          directories which do not correspond to a users name.
Released: 12-Jun-95

0.1062 Fixed two nasty bugs in userbase.library.
Released: 13-Jun-95

0.1063 Recompiled various progs with Nicks new includes.
       mbzeus now generates a ^ROUTE kludge for ZMP if there is a route
          address given in the SaveMessage() call.
       Added rexx command 'WHOSONLINE'. (AB)
       Speeded up ANSI's scrolling by prescanning for \n's in the input
          stream.
       The Control/Gadget system now supports placable icons.  Before adding
          your gadget, set the Gadget->UserData to NULL for floating or
          1 for fixed position.
       Added CC's 225-227, 230-231 and 252.
       Added IR_CHECKMSGS to input modes.
       Added CheckMsgList() and GetLineMsg() to library.
       DLG's BCGet now works!
       DLGDoor now sets ANSI compression (if it's not already on) and clears
          it after.
       Added RedrawEdit() to library.
       Fixed some nasties in the userbase.library which caused problems
          when deleting users. (RK)
       New READ flag: SHOWMSGS.  When specified, node messages (as generated
          by Zeus:Bin/SendMsg for example) are shown DURING the input.  You
          should use the PROMPT command to set your menu prompts from now
          on so Zeus can redraw them after displaying the messages.
       Control only redraws the background when removing gadgets.
       Fixed semaphore bug which caused Control to hang fairly often. (SM)
       Fixed problem in RIP's 'w' command.  Now checks for legal inputs. (GH)
       ANSI now takes a new command line parameter 'JUMPY' to enable
          the new fast pre-scroll routines.
       Fergot to add NP_CopyVars to progs being started up by
          Control/Watchers. (MV)
       Fixed bug in XlkDoor which caused some probs when it couldn't load
          a door. (MV)
       Added new rexx command 'SERINPUT <ON|OFF>'.  Enables/Disables serial
          input from the user.
       CHKUSERSTATS now returns 6 if the user is already online.
Released: 29-Jun-95

0.1077 Fixed a couple of potential bugs in IEMSI.
       Fixed bug in CHKUSERSTATS where it was returning 6 if the user had
          been PUTONLINE!
       Fixed Control redraw bug.
       The library xfer routines now log the results of the xfer.
       HydraXfers logging is now more standard.
Released: 30-Jun-95

0.1088 Finally added the code for the Zeus.key processing.  Do not install
          this new version unless you have your Zeus.key!!
       Added new Rexx command SETDEFRIP - sets the default RIP palette. (GH)
Released: 05-Jul-95

0.1090 Added CC 118.
       Fixed up the ANSI music code.  Note lengths were not being calculated
          properly.
       Zeus won't try and run CLIDoors if there is less than 50k free
          memory. (RK)
       Now checks for the existance of DoorControl and sets a high failat
          level.
       The CLIDoor scripts now have unique names so if a door does hang
          (but Zeus recovers control) then other doors may be run on that
          line.
       Zeus can now recover from totally hung CLIDoors.  This may take up
          to 60 seconds (to allow the door ample time to wake up and quit)
          and will not work 100% but it gives it a go ;)
       Fixed bug where users can type control codes into the input! (GS)
       Added some more carrier checking into XlkDoor.
Released: 09-Jul-95

0.1111 Added some more protection into the CLI door code.  Even if a remote
          caller manages to get into a shell, Zeus will not allow them to
          enter any data.
       Rewrote Bin/Chat to not expand CC's.  The ChatWrite() function is now
          defunct - use WriteLine() instead for more flexability!
       mbuunews now scans past deleted messages. (GS)
       Fixed an IO Torture hit when More? prompts come up in CLIDoors (RK)
       Added more RLT_* tags so ReadLineTags() is now up to date with all
          the new features.
       You can now boot users offline easily with the handy new BootUser()
          library function.
       Bin/TextPreLoad can now recurse through directories.

       Cleaned up and finished (hopefully!) the following:

          Zeus:Bin/System/MailerStart
          Zeus:Bin/System/NetStart
          
          Zeus:Bin/BBSLine
          Zeus:Bin/BM
          Zeus:Bin/BootUser
          Zeus:Bin/Chat
          Zeus:Bin/mbManager
          Zeus:Bin/SendMsg        <- Check out the previously undocumented
                                     options!!
          Zeus:Bin/UserManager

          Zeus:Prefs/Bulletins
Released: 24-Jul-95

0.1113 Added SetCLIMore() function to set More? prompts on/off from within
          CLIDoors.  DLGDoor now uses this!
       ChatStatus now stores it's status in ENV(ARC):ChatStatus so it will
          remember it's last setting even through a reset.
       ChatStatus now takes arguments to place it's icon on the control
          screen.
       Fixed problems in mbzeus with the maint functions.
       ANSI now takes XPOS/YPOS arguments for it's icon.
       Went through lots of progs adding version strings!!!
       Added some new powerfull control codes to the menu code!  See
          MenuEditing.doc for info!
       Included some example ANSI music fun of my own creation!  Drop to
          a ZShell, turn your speakers up REAL loud and enter
          'Type Zeus:Text/Music/Gringo.txt' =o)

       Cleaned up and finished (hopefully!) the following:

          Zeus:Bin/System/DoorControl
          Zeus:Bin/Watchers/ANSI

          Zeus:Libs/mbzeus.library
          Zeus:Libs/userbase.library
          
          Zeus:Prefs/LineEditor
          Zeus:Prefs/MenuEditor
          Zeus:Prefs/Progs
          Zeus:Prefs/System

          Zeus:Utils/ChatStatus
          Zeus:Utils/Logger

Released: 26-Jul-95

0.1119 XprXfer now stops a transfer when the users time runs out. (GH)
       Zeus is now a commodity!  This gets rid of the vaguely annoying
          window/icon it used to have.  You can now quit Zeus through
          any Commodity Exchange program or via ARexx (as normal). (GH)
       Wrote a replacement to SimpleEd - ZEd.  This line editor uses all
          the standard Zeus command line editing keys and has more useful
          options!  See ZEd.doc for info.
       Zeus can now be shut down with a configurable key combination.  It
          can also take an argument to set the commodity priority (this
          is not the same as Zeus' task priority BTW...)

       Zeus [CX_PRIORITY=<-128 -> 127>] ["HOTKEY=rawkey xxxxx"]

       The default hotkey is Ctrl + Esc and the default priority is zero.
Released: 28-Jul-95

0.1136 Zeus now takes an new argument 'KILLTIME <Seconds>' defaults to 100.
       Fixed line wrap bug in ZEd.
       Fixed enforcers in ChatStatus.
       Fixed 12 hour/24 hour bug in WriteUserLog(). (EO)
       Put the code back into XprXfer to check for already present files.
Released: 03-Aug-95

0.1137 PUSHINPUT is now async.
       Fixed IntuiText part of LayoutGads() to affect positioned gadgets.
       ZShell now disables requesters. (VN)
       Added new read mode: STRIP - Doesn't allow leading or trailing
          spaces.  Excellent for getting user data and the like...
       Fixed intermitant enforcer hits when Zeus closed down.
       When reading in SECRET mode, all the normal editing functions are
          disabled apart from Delete Line (^K) and backspace.  The others
          were causing interesting 'effects'.
       Fixed problem which caused text to disappear when you shift-left
          and then shift-right.
       mbstarmsg.library is now up to date and can be used with mbManager
          to access the maintenance functions.  Zeus:Bin/PostImport is
          now defunct and should be deleted.  I've also put the support
          back in for FTSC, Foozle and TrapToss style saved messages.
       Rewrote Prefs/StarMsgCfg.  When you save the config, it is auto-
          matically updated in real time if Zeus is already running.
       Created new mb*.library function mbCreateWaitingMail() which is used
          with external mail processors.  It scans the new messages in an
          area and creates waiting mail data for users.
       Fixed potential problem where new message areas would have their
          pointers cleared after a 'UpdateConfigs MA'.
       Prefs/InterNet now updates in real-time when you click 'Save'.
       Fixed GetNumberOfMessages() bug in mbuunews.
       Fixed bug in mbuunews which caused all pointers to dissapear when
          you did a 'UpdateConfigs MA'.
Released: 09-Aug-95

0.1140 FINALLY got round to fixing the bug which caused WRITE to crash on
          long strings.  NextArg() was returning max + 1 chars! (NL)
       Increased WRITE's maximum length to 1024.
       StarMsgCfg now opens on the Control screen. (NL)
       mbstarmsg now use the new AddWaitingMail() function so 'mbManager
          WAITINGMAIL' should now work.
       Rewrote Prefs/InterNet.  The flags window has been removed and new
          fields have been added for header porting/kludging and dynamic
          InterNet account support.
       mbuunews now posts messages to the EMail base (if there is one) when
          the newsgroup is moderated.
       Added some new language tags which are used with GETYESNO: (NL)
       
          YESTXT:   [37mYes
          NOTXT:    [37mNo
          CONTTXT:  [37mContinuous
       
       Added BACKGROUND=BG options into Control/ANSI.
       Control now has a lock port so it cannot be started twice.
       Added function GetControlWindow() to library. (NL)
       Started ZGate - the InterNet <-> Zeus <-> FidoNet Gateway prog which
          handles E-Mail/NetMail conversion even through dynamic InterNet
          accounts!
       Made a new config prog that defines users names/aliases and their
          fidonet addresses.  This will not only allow ZMP to remap netmails
          to points and define addresses for use with ZGate but it will
          also keep Gavin happy =o)
       ZMP: Fixed problem with MM generated SEEN-BY/PATH lines. (DN)
       ZMP: Global NETEXECs were not being freed.
       ZMP: When GATEMAIL is specified, netmails addressed to your system
          will not be bounced if the user doesn't exist but the To: field
          has a '@' in it.
       ZMP: May have found the Update Config crash problem. (PB/KG)
       ZMP: When a netmail comes into your system, the To: field is
          checked against the User Map config and routed if a matching
          address is found.
       ZMP: When a system has paused an area but they receive a message
          addressed to them (from the User Map config) then that message
          is exported.
       Redesigned Prefs/InterNet AGAIN - Now has lots more options!!
Released: 22-Aug-95

0.1145 Prefs/Mapper and Prefs/InterNet now ask you if you want to save the
          config if it's been changed. (NL)
       Control/ANSI/RIP do not try to iconify when there are other windows
          open on their screens. (RK)
       XprXfer now truncates the file name if it is too large and clears
          the error message field when it opens a new file. (SR)
       Load/SaveUserXData() now check for null length user names.
       The 'Protocol:' text in XprXfer was 8 pixels out!  Didn't anyone
          notice???
       Fixed a couple of script bugs in ZAmiMirror.rexx and TreeToCfg.rexx
       ZMP can now parse 2, 3, 4, or 5 dimensional SEEN-BY and PATH lines
          although it still only writes 2d or 3d ones.
       Added new ZMP config keywords, ALLOWMIXEDPKT and NOECHOCREATE.
       Added line number field to Watcher Messages. (NL)
       Added a file TICK into ZMP!!  Had to mess about with the SYSTEM
          lines again (sorry!) but there is a conversion script in this
          update.
       Added a HATCH into ZMP!!!  Run 'ZMP Hatch'...
       Rescanning individual echos is now done with %RESCAN <TagName>.
       Added TICK area support into AreaFix.
       TICK areas can now be auto-created.
       Added NEWTICKAREA, AUTOTICKADD, AUTOECHOADD, NOTICKCREATE and
          TICKFMT keywords to ZMP.cfg.
       When remapping netmails, ZMP now strips all kludge lines from the
          top of the message and adds a new INTL and, if needed, TOPT and
          FMPT kludges.  This will stop duping problems and routing errors
          due to wrong INTL/etc lines...
       If you have multiple names in a Mapper entry, you can prefix ONE of
          the names with a '@' and when a netmail gets remapped, that name
          will be used in the To: field.
       Have fun with that lot!!! :)
Released: 29-Aug-95

0.1146 ChatStatus can now be run from the workbench since it has a natty
          new icon!
       Optimized ZMP's address parsing routine.
       AreaFix now checks the length of commands (was overwriting stack on
          very long ones!) (MH)
       ZMP now adds the last address on the PATH lines to the SEEN-BY lines
          (if it doesn't already exist) to solve problems with braindead
          E! packets. (GC)
       ZMP's hatch didn't add the REPLACE keyword into TIC files!
       Added CC 99 for number of days till a user expires. (PB)
       Prefs/Mapper now opens its requesters on the same screen as its
          window. (AB)
       Optimized ZMP's config reading a bit.
       ZMP can now not send *.TIC files to systems.  On the SYSTEM lines,
          set the TIC FLO type to lower case to disable TIC files. (AB)
       Fixed BOLD bug in ANSI. (PB)
       Added twitting into ZMP.  New keywords: TWITUSER and TWITADDR.
       *Might* have found the bug which causes random outbound packets to
          appear in the inbound!
Released: 10-Sep-95

0.1147 Added some new options into ChatStatus and Logger.
       You need to copy Zeus:Utils/Logger.info Zeus:Config/Icons/
       Added a new library function ResetEdit() into zeus.library.
       ZMP's Hatch wasn't adding the origins address to the SeenBys!!!
       Logger can now be started from the workbench.
       Added a one pixel space between the icons on the Control screen
          and their text (if any).
Released: 11-Sep-95

0.1147 Fixed some Enforcers in ChatStatus.
       Added CC's 302 and 303.
       Removed ARCNETMAIL keyword from ZMP.cfg.
       SYSTEM lines now need another flag for Arc Netmail Y/N.
       Added MAXPKTSIZE <Addresses> into ZMP.
       Added access field to text and script filenames.  See revised
          TextSystem.doc for info.
       Fixed point problem in ZMP.
       Added CC's 304-312, 253.
       Edit functions now filter out ^L.
       Added language tag 'USERLOGDATEFMT' for formating the date part of
          the users Event.log.
       Added ADDHIST and USEHIST to READ.
       Added CLEARHISTORY to Rexx.
       When 'Count Local Calls' is off, PUTONLINE was not increasing the
          number of calls in the user structure.
       Added auto-hatch into ZMP.
Released: 16-Sep-95

0.1156 Hatch/Tick now add time zone information to TIC path lines if
          available.  Do a 'SetEnv TZ GMT' (or whatever your time zone is)
          and then 'Copy ENV:TZ ENVARC:TZ'.
       Fixed CC 306 bug. (RK)
       If ZMP was adding a file to a FLO which was already listed, it was
          not returning TRUE!
       Edit functions now strip out all characters < 0x20 apart from ones
          that Zeus uses.
       Fixed a buggy rename routine in ZMP.
Released: 19-Sep-95

0.1163 Fixed Enforcer in GetConnectModes().
       Changed the InterNet configuration structures.  (Gee..  Hope no one
          was using those 'cept me :) )
       Added GetINetCfg()/FreeINetCfg() to library.
       Fixed LockPubScreen() usage in XprXfer.
       Zeus now assumes that users have 24 lines on their screen before
          their account has been PUTONLINE.
       Control/ANSI/RIP now use Amiga '?' for About (Makes all the
          difference apparently :)
       Added WM_UPDATEUSER to Watcher Message types.
       ANSI/RIP now update their title bars on receipt of a WM_UPDATEUSER
          message.
       Zeus sends a WM_UPDATEUSER message every minute while the user is
          online (shows time left).
       WM_UPDATEUSER messages also get sent when you call SAVEUSER and
          SETUSERDATA.
       When Control is in the window state, the LayoutGads() function was
          not setting the gadgets font properly.
       Control now calls LayoutGads() when its window is resized.
       Fixed wrong return code in one of the internal maint functions in
          mbzeus.
       ZMP will now try to append to existing outbound packets found in
          the PACKDIR.
Released: 25-Sep-95

0.1170 You can now customise the watcher title bars!  See the example
          Zeus:Config/Watchers/Titles.cfg to see how it works.  You may
          use up to 10 titles.
       Rearranged the watcher menus a bit.  Added 'Reload Titles' to update
          the watcher title prefs.
       BBSLine now takes an optional argument to specify the name of the
          startup script.  I.e. 'BBSLine 0 Local.zeus'.
       Cleaned up MenuEditor - vanilla keys now work and it detects
          duplicate COMMKEYs...
       Control now adds itself as a watcher on line -1 and responds to
          WM_ICONIFY, WM_UNICONIFY, WM_TOFRONT, WM_TOBACK & WM_QUIT.
       Zeus now takes a new argument 'QUITCONTROL' which will try and
          shut down Control (and anything else linked into line -1) when
          Zeus is closing.
       Modified XprXfer a little to try and solve the crashes, let me
          know if it works!
Released: 26-Sep-95

0.1172 Fixed filename length bug in XprXfer.
       ZMP now starts archivers at the same priority as itself.
       Fixed prob in BBSLine with the default startup script name.
       Fixed missing filename problem in XprXfer.
       Improved ordering of Watcher adding!
       Logging of xfers now show if it is an upload or download session.
       XprXfer doesn't uniconify the watcher when started (Never found
          what was causing it, but after fixing some other bugs, I tested
          it and it STAYED iconified ;)
       (Yet another) Redesign of Prefs/InterNet with all the needed info
          for ZGate.
       Fixed hourly timer bug that caused users to be chucked off.
       Fixed ZMP's HATCH argument parsing.
       Fixed problem in ZMP when exporting null length messages.
       
       Sorry about the lack of development at the moment - been setting up
          some web pages for GreenPeace to protest about the French nuclear
          tests in Mururoa!!  Back to work next week with some InterNet
          docs!!!

Released: 11-Oct-95

0.1174 Control wasn't sending a WM_UNICONIFY message!
       The CLI Door Handler was really not handling the ACTION_READ packet
          very well when it came to short reads!
       Added a flags field into the WatcherMsg structure.
       SignalWatchers() now takes an additional flags argument.
       Renamed Shared->Ver_PL to Shared->ZVer and Shared->Rev_PL to
          Shared->ZRev.
       Changed the door handlers dos entry from PLDH: to ZDH:
       Increased several internal buffers, including the le->le_Status one
          which is now 256 bytes instead of 50!
       Recompiled everything for these changes!
       BBSLine doesn't change it's task name to the current ARexx command
          name anymore unless you specify the TRACE argument.
       Removed Node/Domain fields from InterNet cfg and replaced it with
          a single Address field.  You'll need to delete your
          Zeus:Config/InterNet.dat again I'm afraid :(
Released: 17-Oct-95

0.1194 Revamped some very dodgy code in NetStart!
       Prefs/InterNet had a very low max limit on it's Indexes field!
       Added CC's 189 & 190.
       Fixed template bug in mbManager.
       Added EXPIRES to Get/SetUserData.
       ZMP now uses ReadArgs().
       Cleaned up some internal debug stuff in ZMP.
       Added a few more bits into ZGate.
       Ok, so ExpandCCStr() wasn't null terminating the result - shoot me!
       Released some InterNet docs - not completed but there's a fair
          wodge of useful info to keep you all happy :)
Released: 25-Oct-95

0.1198 Fixed bug in ZMP where all messages were logged in ZShovel.log!
       Fixed nasty history bug in ZShell.
       Zeus' status window will now open on the Control screen if
          available.
Released: 25-Oct-95

0.1198 Moved XprXfer's "Filename:" text down one pixel - twasn't level!
       Fixed Enforcer hit in XprXfer when Filesize field was updated
          before the file was opened.
       During a send, XprXfer now shows the files size even if the protocol
          doesn't supply it.  I.e. Xmodem...
       On an aborted/failed session XprXfer now sends several ^X chars to
          quit the other side.  It also performs a CMD_CLEAR after each
          xfer.
       Fixed very old bug in the pipe routines which filled them up with
          undeletable data!!
       Wrote my very own nullmodem device which uses the Zeus pipe and
          edit library routines!  It's name is znm.device...
       Fixed some problems with mbzeus' maint and trim functions.
Released: 03-Nov-95

0.1201 Added line messages based on how many minutes the user has left.
          For example, to send a message when the user has five, two and
          one minute left, add the following tags to your language files:

          TIMELEFT5:     [31mYou only have 5 minutes left!!\n
          TIMELEFT2:     [31mYou only have 2 minutes left!!\n
          TIMELEFT1:     [31mYou only have 1 minutes left - BYE!!\n

       Fixed enfocer in znm.device during answer.
       XprXfer now takes advantage of the XPR 2.001 double buffering
          feature!  May speed up transfers a bit.
       Also put asynch file read/writing routines into XprXfer.
       Recompiled ZMP with Nicks new headers.
Released: 06-Nov-95

0.1204 Added CC 313.
       The SavedData information is now saved to a temporary file and then
          renamed to prevent data loss.
       Added some extra saved data (Shared->Extra) which contain information
          about how long Zeus has been active and online.
       Changed Zeus' version string from Pipeline!
       Zeus now saves the Saved/Extra data every hour.
       Added CC's 140-145.
       Added new borderless option to Control.  Selectable from the Prefs
          menu.
       Totally re-wrote Utils/SysUsage to take advantage of the new extra
          saved information.  3d look, sizable and it updates 'n' all!!
       MenuEditors Save/Save As menu options were perminently disabled!
       Prefs/InterNet was not opening it's requesters on the right screen.
       ZMP was creating archives of pass-through mail in the UNPACKDIR when
          MAXPKTSIZE was in effect.
       Wrote another new stats program called 'TimeStat' - Shows Zeus'
          uptime and how much of that time users are online.
       Renamed SysUsage to CallerStat.
       ZMP's importing now uses asynch routines!
       Added Tick summary to ZMP.
       Speeded up mbzeus' trim and maintenance routines with asynch stuff
          and some other tricks!
       mbzeus' trim and maintenance functions now checks if the message
          text position is actually within the bounds of the text data file.
          If not, the message is deleted.
       Removed 0x9b (Amiga CSI) removal routines from Read/Write since it's
          used in the Greek character set.
Released: 09-Nov-95

0.1210 Improved ZMP's TIC file parsing.
       ZMP TICK now deletes the replaced file (if any) before checking for
          dupes!
       mbzeus' mbEditMessage() will now try to append the message text to
          the end of the file if there is a problem writing over the old
          message.
       mbzeus' trim function should now be a bit faster since it does less
          checking in the text file, although it now has to scan the header
          file twice.
       mbzeus' mbLoadMessage() now respects the LM_NEXTMSG flag.
       ZMPs tick summary had the tag name right justified instead of left!
       Rewrote mbzeus' maintenance function (again!) so it really tries to
          rescue a demented msg base!  It takes ages (so I wouldn't
          recommend running it daily on all bases) but if you have a base
          causing problems, try it out.  It will attempt to rescan the base
          and revive any corrupted messages.  This can result in message
          headers and text not matching up or 1-4 strange characters at the
          beginning of the message text (but I can't really prevent this!)
          Any msgs with their text in the right place will be quite safe
          and serve as pointers for finding corrupt messages.
       Speeded up ZMPs config reading routines.
       Fixed ZMP hatch bug where it wouldn't always send the file to every
          system.
       ZMP tick was incrementing the imported tick files counter by two
          for every file!
       Implemented the GATEBATCH routines in ZGate.
       When reloading the InterNet configuration with LoadINetCfg( TRUE ),
          zeus.library wasn't freeing the old headers/access lists!
       You can now specify whether ZGate should Port/Kludge/Delete all
          header lines by default.
       Pressing 'S' in the InterNet configuration was saving the config to
          disk but not re-loading it into the zeus.library!
       Added a big ol' import summary to ZMP which shows a complete run
          down of what went on.  It's so big that it's only written to the
          ZMP.log file since it is too wide for a normal Shell window :)
Released: 14-Nov-95

0.1211 Fixed ZMPs tick report.
       ZMPs tick now parses stupid PC generated tick files with more than
          one SeenBy address on a line.
       Revamped the codes you can use in ZMPs NETEXEC commands.  They are
          as follows:

          %f - Who the message is from
          %t - Who the message is to
          %s - The subject of the message (Usually password but could be
                  other data!)
          %A - The from address of the message (Zone:Net/Node.Point)
          %D - The dest address of the message (Zone:Net/Node.Point)
          %n - The number of the saved message
          %a - The area the message was saved into
          %% - A '%' character

       ZMP wasn't calculating the message length properly for netmails
          without an AREA:MATRIX line.
       Added CC 314.
       Added some status information to ZGate GATEBATCH.
       ZMP now filenotes bad packets/archives/ticks describing what was
          wrong.
       XprXfer now sets the line status to show what files the user is
          uploading/downloading.
       Added snappy export summary to ZMP.
       Found a semphore bug in SignalWatchers() which would have caused
          some nasty things to happen if it was called more than once at
          the same time and some watcher returned WR_MOVETOTOP/BOT.
       CallerStat wasn't updating the caller averages and info box
          properly!
       CallerStat/TimeStat now die when Zeus does.
       ZMP now does tick/hatch zone gating!
       If you receive netmails with your mail packets/ticks attached, ZMP
          will still import the netmail but won't move the files out of the
          inbound.
Released: 16-Nov-95

0.1212 Added s'more NETEXEC codes:

          %F - Who the message is from (with underscores)
          %T - Who the message is to (with underscores)
          %S - The subject of the message (with underscores)

       Fixed bug in Prefs/InterNet where if you had the gate type set to
          private, you couldn't click on the gate access list.
       When XprXfer sets the line status to show what file is being xfered,
          it only uses the filename and cuts out the path.
       ZGates' GATEBATCH is more robust at coping with errors!
       Added CTRL-C breaking to ZGate when doing a GATEBATCH.
Released: 18-Nov-95

0.1213 Fixed problem with blank lines in AreaFix requests.
       READ wasn't resetting the history list on an error.
       Abberexxs' CLS command now resets the ANSI colours/styles as well.
       Fixed problem in ZMP with netmail processing.  It was prefixing
          the message text with a CR!
       Fixed AreaFix problems.
       AreaFix now handles netmails that begin with AREA:MATRIX (without
          a 0x01 kludge)
Released: 21-Nov-95

0.1213 Fixed problems in the watcher signal functions.
       Improved znm.device's CONNECT code since TrapDoor was having some
          troubles with it!
       ZMP was exported to unlinked write-only systems!
       ANSI now sends a WM_UNICONIFY message when it opens its screen.
       New config entry in ZMP.cfg: TICDIR <dirname> - directory to store
          #?.TIC files in.  Defaults to your outbound dir.
       Fixed bug in ZMP with unlinked flags.
       XprXfer/HydraXfer now respects the custom Upload Directory setting.
       ZMP doesn't load the archivers config in anymore, it reads it from
          the zmf's internal list.
       Added a batch hatch option to ZMP.
       Zeus has now got it's own FTSC product code (258) which ZMP now puts
          into the packet headers it generates.
       GetGad() now sets the returned gadgets Flags field to show the
          alternate image if present.  If no other image data is available,
          the gadget is set to complement mode.
       GetGad() also fills the Activation field to GACT_RELVERIFY.
       Recompiled ANSI/ChatStatus to take advantage of the new GetGad()
          bits...
       DoorControl now sets the correct ProgramDir for CLIDoors.
       Zeus now takes more care when saving the bulletins!
       
       Hope yawl had a merry chrimble and lets hope it's gunna be a ZEUSY
          new year!!
Released: 03-Jan-96

0.1214 Fixed problem in ZMP which meant that the archiver extract string
          didn't have un-used tilde codes stripped out.
       Fixed problem with TICDIR.
       Removed password CC.
       Rewrote large portions of ZGate to get some speed up!
       ZGate now processes mailing lists.
       Fixed GETSTATUS.
       ZMP was creating .?LO files in the TICDIR!
       Fixed ANSI/RIP argument parsing code a bit.
       When ANSI is run without a config, it attempts to open the IBM.font
          before falling back to topaz.
       RIP now checks to see if the machine it is running on supports the
          NTSC screen mode before using it.
       Control wasn't cloning the default public screen when it couldn't
          load its config.
       Control now opens a screen mode requester BEFORE it opens its screen
          if the ModeID in the config file is not available.
       Sorted out Connectors argument parsing.
       Added icon XPOS/YPOS arguments to Connector.
       Improved the way XprXfer figures out the CPS.  Should now give more
          accurate (and higher!!) results.
       Added database of FidoNet product codes to the zeus.library.  This
          is just so ZMP and ZMailer can look flash :)
       ZMP was generating 1 & 45 headers with a 0xFE product code.  Should
          be 0xFF!!
       ZMP's TICK wasn't respecting the 'no tic' settings, although HATCH
          was...
       Ok, and just to round off this update, ZMAILER - the first release!
Released: 18-Jan-96

0.1217 Fixed many bugs in ZMailers Xpr code!
       ZGate now handles mailing lists which don't have a To: field.
       Added a debug mode into ZMailer to monitor what gets sent/received.
          Run ZMailer <Line Number> DEBUG to get some huge log files :)
       Hopefully fixed ZMPs buggy packet generating problems.
       ZMPs AreaFix Tick list wasn't showing which areas were linked.
       Fixed %QUERY command for Tick areas.
       Added OwnDevUnit.library support to ZMailer.  If the library is
          available, ZMailer will use it.
       Wrote a ZMailer Rexx script to run programs using OwnDevUnit's
          functions.
       Found a fairly major bug in ZMailer's EMSI code - should work a
          lot better now!!
       Fixed Enforcer hits when ZMailer was iconified.
Released: 21-Jan-96

0.1217 Fixed hydra bug in ZMailer which was putting 'Sending file...' in 
          the name field instead of the message field!!
       Fixed 'serial busy' report due to a SDCMD_SETPARAMS call in ZMailer.
       Fixed minor bug in inbound filename bumping!
       ZMailer's CALL rexx function now accepts phone numbers as well as
          node addresses.
       Added 'QUIT' rexx function to ZMailer.
       Added XPOS and YPOS arguments to ZMailer for it's Control icon.
       Now ZMailer properly handles non-Fast EMSI handshaking when calling
          out. This was the reason it wasn't connecting to XMailer!
       Many other small tweaks and fixes to ZMailer!!!
Released: 22-Jan-96

0.1217 Fixed Hydra filename receiving bug with XMailer.
       Fixed EMSI handshake problems with some mailers.
       ZMailer now closes it's logfile after every call although DEBUG mode
          tends to keep it open during the idle state.
       Fixed field lengths in ZMailer window.
       ZMailer now uses Text() instead of PrintIText() which not only
          removes all those OpenFont() calls, but should also speed up the
          display a bit.
       ZMP will no longer clone Netmail areas when generating new Echomail
          areas!
Released: 26-Jan-96

0.1218 Added new ARexx command SETSCRDIR [Dir] - sets the current script
          directory used by the line process.  Give a null argument to
          default to the dir set in Prefs/System.
       Added new value that may be passed to AddWatcher() - AW_ALLLINES.
          This will send your message port a copy of all watcher messages
          on all lines.
       Fixed misplaced check carrier call in ZMailer!
Released: 27-Jan-96

0.1220 SignalWatchers() now uses AttemptSemaphore() instead of Obtain to
          prevent blocking problems.  It returns TRUE if the signal was
          done.
       Fixed the layout of LineEditor's Access window and added a new field
          to select what kind of logon restrictions to use.
       Edited various bits of Zeus:Zeus to use the above changes.
       Prefs/LineEditor can now update the online configuration.  It won't
          add or delete lines but for changing modem strings and access
          times it's very useful.
       ZMailer now respects the Mail-Only and No-Answer settings in the
          LineEditor config.  All the other settings are handled by the
          BBS since you can set users to be unrestricted.
       ZMailer now supports logging to the Line-x.log files, logging
          caller ID data, and you can specify under what conditions the
          after session script should be run.
       Found a nice bug in the Xpr code of ZMailer - it wasn't letting
          the xpr library know about the current serial settings!
       XprXfer now tells the xpr libraries the real baud rate instead of
          the locked one.
Released: 02-Feb-96

0.1221 Oops!  Just discovered that line access stuff wasn't working quite
          as well as it could've been!  Fixed in Zeus & ZMailer.
       Improved ZMailers xpr setup code!
Released: 02-Feb-96

0.1221 Implemented Hydra8k & Hydra16k protocols into ZMailer.  Hydra8k kicks
          in on connections of 14400 and uses 4k blocks unless the baud rate
          is 28800+ in which case it uses 8k ones.  Hydra16k uses 12k blocks
          at 28800 and 16k blocks at 38400+.
       Fixed bad hydra bug in the original HydraCom source that wouldn't
          parse the hydra options properly.
       Turns out ZMailer was using some really daft hydra options which
          slowed down the xfer rate considerably!  Should be much faster
          now!
       Fixed ZMailer incompatibility with Xenia mailers which send strange
          0x11 characters for no apparent reason...
Released: 03-Feb-96

0.1223 Fixed some more problems with Hydra.
       Added Hydra8k & Hydra16k switches to ZMailers config.
       Zeus now has a smart new loading logo!  It's currently 8 colours
          with a Magic WB palette but I'll be doing a 4 colour version
          at some point.
       MenuEditors menus are now 'NewLook'.
       Fixed some problems with LASTINPUT.
       Fixed minor enforcer in zeus.library.
Released: 04-Feb-96

0.1225 Fixed file requesters in Control, Bulletins, InterNet and System -
          they weren't opening on the ZEUS screen.
       Hopefully fixed RAW door problems.
       Fixed some NEW problems with LASTINPUT ;)
Released: 05-Feb-96

0.1226 Fixed s'more problems with hydra sending.  Seems to be working
          pretty well here now!
       ZMailer now respects the PUA, PUP, NPU, HAT, HXT, HRQ, NRQ & FNC
          EMSI flags.
       WaZOO & EMSI are now fully implemented in ZMailer.
       Control now sends WM_ICONIFY/UNICONIFY messages when opening/closing
          it's screen.
       Optimised ZMailers Xpr receive a little.
       ANSI now brings up a screen mode requester if the given screen mode
          ID can't be used.
       ZMailer will now respond to window events during sessions although
          the quit and select font options won't work.
       LASTINPUT problems are REALLY fixed now!  Tricky stuff but it's a 
          done thang!
Released: 08-Feb-96

0.1226 Wrote Doors/ABBERexx which is a CNet/Xenolink ARexx door
          interpreter.  It will cover the generic abberexx command set as
          well and replace Zeus' current ABBEREXX function.
       The xenolink.library was still opening the pipeutil.library!
       XlkDoor now looks for .ans files when displaying a file.
       XprXfer doesn't allow users to upload files that already exist in
          the catalogue.
       Wrote a online game statistics generator!  See DoorStats.doc for
          details.
       Finally got round to releasing my user birthdays stuff...
Released: 10-Feb-96

0.1228 Fixed a couple more problems with local/serial character detection.
          Was noticable in ChatPage coz Ron doesn't use the proper Zeus
          chat routines ;o)
       You can now set the speed of input animations by using \s<Delay>
          where <Delay> is 1-4 digits for 100ths of a second delay.
          Note: \s25 is the default.
       ZMailer can now abort sessions.  Pressing the escape key will hang
          up if a mail session is taking place, or reset the modem if not.
       ZMailers fax/voice commands were waiting for a CONNECT message before
          spawning (well, thas the way it works here ;)  Now, as soon as the
          fax/voice string is received, the relevant program is run.
       Fixed that nasty redial problem in ZMailer - sorry to all who had
          problems with it =o{
       Pressing escape in ZMailers window will also abort the current
          redial.
       READ's ANIM argument can now handle language tags AND anim strings
          passed in the script.  Example (with exciting speed settings!!):

          Write '"\n[0;32mPress [[37mRETURN[32m] to continue: [0m"'
          Read Hot NoShow Opts '"\r"' Anim '"\s10[37m[21Dreturn\s25[6DR[CT[CR[4DE[CU[CN[15C"'

       Fixed problem in ZMailer where it occasionally 'forgot' a password
          when calling out!
       ZMailer can now send text files for the Banner and BBS Message text.
          The first character of the text should be a '<' character,
          followed by the full path of the file.
          Example: '<Mail:Banner.txt'
       Added a field to the ZMailer config for a Mail Only message.  This
          is sent during the times you have setup in Prefs/LineEditor for
          mail calls and can be a text file when prefixed with a '<'.
Released: 12-Feb-96

0.1229 ZMailer now detects when files in a .?LO file have no given path and
          looks for them in the outbound dir.
       Found a bad hydra receive bug!  Things should work much better now!
       New fields in ZMailer's Modem settings config:

          Serial Buff - ZMailers internal serial buffer.  If you get serial
                        buffer overflows, try increasing this value.
                        Recommended to be at least 16384.

          EMSI Buff   - Size of buffer for storing EMSI information.  Set
                        to 4096.

          Char Delay  - Some modems can't handle data being sent to them
                        at full speed while in command mode.  This field
                        sets the 50ths of a second ZMailer should wait
                        after sending each character.  Set to 0 if your
                        modem can handle it!

          Long Delay  - Sets the 50ths of a second ZMailer will delay on
                        a tilde (~) character when sending a modem command.
                        Also sets the time that DTR will be dropped for a
                        carat (^) character.  Set to 25.
Released: 13-Feb-96

0.1229 Forgot to recompile all of Prefs/Mailer!  The string window was
          doing some odd things...
       Added TRX support and accounting into ZMailer.
       Fixed bug where you couldn't select ZMailers font anymore!!
       ZMailer now remebers the text written into the window when you
          iconify.
Released: 14-Feb-96

0.1229 Implemented FTSC-1, Modem7, Telink and DietIFNA protocols into
          ZMailer.
       Finished off Prefs/MenuEditor, Prefs/Bulletins, Prefs/InterNet,
          Prefs/LineEditor, Prefs/Progs, Prefs/Mapper, Prefs/System.
       Renamed Prefs/Progs -> Prefs/Startup.  Don't forget to change your
          icons and MenuEditor entries!
       Added Accounting and Watcher Screen options to Prefs/Mailer.
       Finished off Prefs/Mailer!
       Added some more ARexx commmands to ZMailer.  The complete list is:

          AFTERSESSION <Command>       - Sets the after session command
          BANNER <String>              - Sets the banner message
          BBSMESSAGE <String>          - Sets the BBS available message
          CALL <Node|Number>           - Calls a node/phone-number
          CLEARCALLS                   - Clear all redials
          DATAONLINE <String>          - Sets the Data Online string
          FAXHANDLER <Command>         - Sets the fax handler command
          FILEREQUEST <Command>        - Sets the file request command
          FORBID <NONE|XMAIL|FREQ|ALL> - Ask the other system not to send
                                         the specified types of file.
          KEEP <NONE|XMAIL|ALL>        - Sets what files shouldn't be sent
                                         during a mail session.
          MINBAUD <Baud>               - Sets the minimum baud rate for
                                         outgoing connects.
          MODEMINIT <String>           - Sets the modem init string
          MOMESSAGE <String>           - Sets the mail-only message
          PICKUP <ALL|PRIMARY|NONE>    - When dialling out, specify what
                                         should be picked up.
          POSTDIAL <String>            - Sets the post-dial string
          PREDIAL <String>             - Sets the pre-dial string
          QUIT                         - Quits ZMailer
          SMODEM <String>              - Sends the given command to the
                                         modem.
          VOICEHANDLER <Command>       - Sets the voice handler command.

       ZMailer now remembers text written to the window even when it isn't
          open!  Also redraws the text without overwriting the borders!!
Released: 16-Feb-96

                     ***** LAST CALL FOR BUGS!! *****

0.1229 Finally got round to implementing message translation tables into
          ZMP.  You can have one or two tables on both input and output
          for each domain! The keywords are:

          ITRANSLATION <Table1> [Table2]
          OTRANSLATION <Table1> [Table2]

          On import, the text is translated through <Table1> and then, if
          specified, through <Table2>.  It is then saved using the standard
          SaveMessage() call.

          On export, the text is translated through <Table1> and then, if
          specified, through <Table2>.  It is then exported to all connected
          nodes.

          The defined tables affect all areas defined AFTER the keywords.
          This way you can specify different translations for certain areas.
          Example:
          
          NODE   666:666/666.666
          
          ; This area won't use any translation
          
          AREA   SATAN_RULEZ ....
          
          ; Set up some translation
          
          ITRANSLATION Tab1 Tab2
          OTRANSLATION Tab2 Tab1
          
          AREA   HE_DOES_TOO ...
          
          ; Different translation
          
          ITRANSLATION Tab3 Tab4
          OTRANSLATION Tab4 Tab3

          AREA   MY_MUM_TOLD_ME_SO ...
          
       Recompiled ZMP to work with Nicks new monster update!
Released: 20-Feb-96

0.1262 Recompiled mbManager to fix RANGE crash.
       ZMailer now flushes the serial device out of memory when it closes.
       Fixed bug in ZMailer where it would crash with logfile opening probs.
       ZMailer should be reseting properly now!
       Recompiled ZEd for deleting ranges of lines problems...
       Removed ABBEREXX command from Zeus since this is now handled by the
          new external CLIDoor.
       Fixed CC for showing XData.
       Added TrimUserXData() function to zeus.library.
       Speeded up second Hydra batch in ZMailer.
       FINALLY fixed the problems with SignalWatchers() that was causing
          ANSI/Voyeur to hang!!
       
       Why have I not done an update in almost seven weeks?  I've been 
          working on the new exciting Zeus development: ZAPP.  I was
          hoping to have it done by the time this release came out but
          alas!  What with the pressure of having to get everything else
          finished before the World-Of-Amiga show this weekend, ZAPP is
          not quite fully operational.  Therefore, there is a distinct
          lack of docs about it in this update.  Just install as normal
          BUT you must make sure you add the following line to your
          User-Startup (if its not already there):
       
       Assign Devs: Zeus:Devs ADD

       Zeus now requires the zeuszapp.device to be around else no one will
          be able to log onto your BBS.  Once you've installed this update
          make sure you reset!
          
       Please don't be asking me about how to try out ZAPP - I'll get a
          proper set of docs and working devices out next week so just
          hold stumm till then please - I've got plenty of other things
          to work on right now :(
Released: 10-Apr-96

